      "role": "user",
      "content": "idk, it doesn't feel like a \"reset.\" a reset implies there's actual potential for a different outcome. but when you look at the variables—the timing, the resources, my own patterns—the trajectory is basically a straight line down. it's not a mistake or a bad math problem, it's just the natural conclusion of the system. honestly, it feels more logical to just accept that the collapse is the only inevitable part left.",
